```plaintext
0result.sql
```

Reason:  
Among the three alternatives, 0result.sql is the only one that  

1. Calculates packing‑time as the interval between order_approved_at and order_delivered_carrier_date – the real period the seller controls – whereas 1result.sql uses the shipping‑limit target and 2result.sql uses the whole purchase‑to‑carrier window.  
2. Computes the average review score once per order (uses DISTINCT order_id) so the rating of a single order is not multiplied by the number of items it contained; the other two over‑weight big orders.  
3. Applies the “> 100 items sold” rule before any further joins, guaranteeing that no seller below the threshold leaks into later steps.  
4. Derives each seller’s top English category with a proper ROW_NUMBER filter.  

Because it meets every business requirement with the cleanest and most accurate logic, 0result.sql is the correct choice.